From: Deividas Nastajus <16858119+dns54@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 12:45:40 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 17/25] UefiPayloadPkg: Open the boot menu when nothing can be
 booted

When no boot option could be launched, BDS calls
PlatformBootManagerUnableToBoot() and then loops forever. Ours returned
right away, so a machine without a bootable disk sat on the logo with no
message and no way into setup: the "Enter Setup" option is an
application, which BDS doesn't boot on its own, and the Esc hotkey is
only read while a boot option is about to start.

Open the boot manager menu instead, the same menu that Esc opens, as
OvmfPkg does. Leaving the menu opens it again.

Signed-off-by: Deividas Nastajus <16858119+dns54@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 .../PlatformBootManagerLib/PlatformBootManager.c    | 13 ++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/UefiPayloadPkg/Library/PlatformBootManagerLib/PlatformBootManager.c b/UefiPayloadPkg/Library/PlatformBootManagerLib/PlatformBootManager.c
index 749c23dbee..034cef0b8e 100644
--- a/UefiPayloadPkg/Library/PlatformBootManagerLib/PlatformBootManager.c
+++ b/UefiPayloadPkg/Library/PlatformBootManagerLib/PlatformBootManager.c
@@ -818,5 +818,16 @@ PlatformBootManagerUnableToBoot (
   VOID
   )
 {
-  return;
+  EFI_BOOT_MANAGER_LOAD_OPTION  BootManagerMenu;
+
+  //
+  // Show the menu that Esc opens instead of a silent logo. Leaving it comes back here.
+  //
+  if (EFI_ERROR (EfiBootManagerGetBootManagerMenu (&BootManagerMenu))) {
+    return;
+  }
+
+  for ( ; ;) {
+    EfiBootManagerBoot (&BootManagerMenu);
+  }
 }
